@startuml CloudWarehouse_Sequence_Rule_RAG
title Value Added — Built-in Rule RAG (Retrieve → Augment → Generate)

actor "Warehouse Admin" as User
participant "index.html\n规则 RAG" as UI
participant "AssistantController" as AC
participant "QuoteAssistantService" as QA
participant "KeywordRetriever\n(TF-IDF + boosts)" as Ret
participant "KnowledgeBaseLoader" as KB
participant "Optional LLM\n(OpenAI if ApiKey)" as LLM
note right of QA
  Built-in **Rule RAG** (lexical).
  Assistive FAQ only.
  Score below MinScore => retrieval-miss.
  Does NOT call FeeCalculationEngine
  or mutate PriceRules / BillLines.
end note

User -> UI : ask question\n(or click preset chip)
UI -> AC : POST /api/Assistant/ask\n{ question, topK }
activate AC
AC -> QA : AskAsync(request)
activate QA

== 1. Retrieve ==
QA -> Ret : Retrieve(query, topK)
activate Ret
Ret -> KB : Load() markdown chunks
activate KB
KB --> Ret : KnowledgeChunk[]
deactivate KB
Ret --> QA : ranked hits + scores
deactivate Ret

alt no hits or score < MinScore
  QA --> AC : mode=retrieval-miss\npipeline=[retrieve,miss]\ngrounded=false
else

== 2. Augment ==
QA -> QA : build citations\n(source, title, score, snippet)

== 3. Generate ==
  alt OpenAI ApiKey configured
    QA -> LLM : chat.completions\n(context = top chunks)
    activate LLM
    LLM --> QA : grounded answer
    deactivate LLM
    QA --> AC : mode=optional-llm\npipeline=[retrieve,augment,generate-llm]\n+ citations
  else default (no paid API)
    QA --> AC : mode=kb-extractive\npipeline=[retrieve,augment,generate-extractive]\n+ citations
  end
end

AC --> UI : ApiResponse\nAssistantAskResponse
deactivate QA
deactivate AC
UI -> User : show RAG pipeline steps\n+ answer + citation cards

@enduml

' Viva one-liner:
' "This is a built-in rule RAG for FAQ — not AI billing; FeeCalculationEngine remains system of record."
